Keep the built-in sensor registrations across the sensor teardown.

The legacy aksensor and the new ak-cam-sensor both call
ispdrv_remove_all_sensors() from their remove paths, wiping the ISP
sensor registry that the CONFIG_SENSOR_* drivers populated at boot.
Unbinding the legacy host, or replacing the new subdev, then leaves the
registry empty and sensor_init fails with -ENODEV. The registry belongs
to the ISP core, not to either subdev, so drop the calls.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/soc_camera/plat-anyka/ak_sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/soc_camera/plat-anyka/ak_sensor.c
@@ -601,6 +601,4 @@ static int aksensor_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 	kfree(priv);
 
-	ispdrv_remove_all_sensors();
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
--- a/drivers/media/platform/anyka/ak-cam-sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/anyka/ak-cam-sensor.c
@@ -409,7 +409,6 @@ static int ak_cam_sensor_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 	kfree(priv);
 
-	ispdrv_remove_all_sensors();
 	cur_sensor_info = NULL;
 
 	return 0;
 }
